       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than double the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. The single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. At this dose there is a serious risk of acute liver injury and failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual ceiling)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **3,000 mg/day total**, divided differently\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 3000 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical rationale. I would still want to confirm it with pharmacy before entering it."
